## Engineering update

The [course's engineering update](https://hq.mega.dev/challenges/what-it-shows), observed
on 28 October, reports that #4471 closed on 5 October. Its two causes have different
outcomes. Close the parser ticket as completed. Close the hint ticket as not planned;
retiring the form is not a hint patch.

<OutcomeTable />

The parser update is `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`. The hint outcome is
`WON'T FIX`, with the reason `booking-v3 form retired`. These are the desk's reported
engineering outcomes. This repository contains the support review, not the production
implementation or independent production test results.

## What changed from the review

The [signed cause review](/kb/decisions/0002-dedupe-by-cause) identified two real defects
and kept the tickets open while the only available account said a fix was queued.
After the course accepted those tickets, refreshing the challenge page revealed the
engineering update. That new evidence supports closure with different reasons.

The accepted decision remains unchanged. Its cause-based triage policy still applies.
The [old incident](/kb/incidents/4471) and its “known / one fix queued” prose describe
the earlier state, not the current engineering disposition. This outcome page adds
the later evidence without rewriting the historical records.

## Evidence and limits

Counts still come from the 4 October export, deduplicated by report ID and classified
with the supplied code and tenant directory. The closure update does not change those
counts. `evidence/analysis.json` records all assigned IDs; the source update is retained
in `src/lib/data/desk-update-2026-10-05.json`.

The five unusual time-related descriptions flagged in the review remain evidence
limitations. The engineering update does not give per-report investigations for them.
Closure follows the desk's stated disposition; it does not independently establish
their root causes or prove that every affected booking was corrected.

